# TDD enforcement rules

# TDD enforcement rules (always active)

- Red → Green → Refactor. Write the failing test, show it fail, write the
  minimum code to pass, show it pass, then refactor with tests green.
- Never edit a test to make it pass unless the PRD's acceptance criterion
  changed — and then update the PRD in the same session.
- Every acceptance criterion in a PRD maps to at least one named test,
  recorded in docs/20-testing/TEST-MAP.md.
- Run the full suite before declaring any feature done.
- Bugs get a failing regression test before the fix.
- Coverage is targeted, not blanket: core logic, APIs, data integrity, and
  anything that was ever the site of a bug are always tested; thin UI glue
  may be exempted only if TEST-MAP.md records the exemption and why.
